WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.069
-We're here with Tina Fey,
and we were talking

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.738
about Restless Leg --
the Restless Leg Tour.

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:06.205
You are doing the Beacon Theatre

00:00:06.205 --> 00:00:08.374
here in New York City
with our friend Amy Poehler.

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:09.608
There's the art for
Restless Leg.

00:00:09.608 --> 00:00:11.578
-That's Amy.
-That's Amy.

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:14.113
And do you guys still --
Do people still

00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:15.948
accidentally call you Amy?

00:00:15.948 --> 00:00:18.918
-Uh...yeah.
-Okay.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:20.386
But the Beacon is a beautiful
theater here in New York City.

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:21.554
You're going
to do a lot of shows.

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.322
You're doing a show
on Super Bowl Sunday.

00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:24.423
-Yes. You pointed
that out to me,

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:25.592
which I thought was so funny.

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:27.793
So, we are doing --
We're coming to New York.

00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:30.362
We're sitting down for,
I want to say, 11 nights.

00:00:30.362 --> 00:00:31.831
-Which is fantastic.
-Which is fantastic.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:34.733
We may be -- We may actually be
setting some kind of record

00:00:34.733 --> 00:00:39.005
for most consecutive nights
of a comedy tour

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:42.608
at the Beacon
by two white women.

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:45.544
-Wow! That's pretty.

00:00:45.544 --> 00:00:48.681
-They're gonna put all that
on a plaque.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:51.451
-You and Amy, I would imagine,
as collaborators --

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.753
I'm familiar with
how well you work together,

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:56.956
but there are still things
you vehemently disagree on.

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:59.592
-Well, there are very
few things we disagree on.

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:02.161
Like, people, in fact --
People often ask us --

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:04.230
We do a Q&amp;A
sometimes in our show,

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.499
and a question
we always get asked is,

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:07.733
"What do you guys fight about?

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:08.768
What do you two fight about?"

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:10.403
And it's kind of
a sexist question, right?

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:11.637
Like, "What do you guys
fight about?"

00:01:11.637 --> 00:01:12.971
And we really don't fight.

00:01:12.971 --> 00:01:15.174
And there's very few things
that we disagree about,

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:17.243
and one of them,
we've discovered,

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:21.648
is that Amy hates Halloween
and I love Halloween.

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:23.016
-I'm shocked.
-Yeah.

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.316
She's, like -- She doesn't
like the aesthetic of it.

00:01:24.316 --> 00:01:25.985
-I'm shocked you like it.

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.320
-Well, yeah, I don't --

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:31.891
I like corny-mom
HomeGoods Halloween.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.859
-Got it.
-Like, basic-bitch Halloween.

00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:35.594
-Okay. Oh, I see.

00:01:35.594 --> 00:01:37.497
Not like -- You don't
want to actually scare anyone.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.499
-No, I don't want
anything scary to happen.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:42.568
I want, like -- I have little,
like, light-up boxes that say

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:45.838
like, "A witch lives here
with her two little monsters."

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:48.474
And Amy's like, "Boo!"

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:51.511
And, so, you know, there have
been times where I'll send her,

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:52.678
like, stuff that
I have in my house,

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:53.813
and she's like, "I hate that.

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.281
Get it out of your house."

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:56.782
So what I thought
I could maybe do here is,

00:01:56.782 --> 00:02:01.053
I would like to show you
some of the things that I own,

00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:03.389
and then you tell me
if I'm crazy,

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.757
because she says,
like, you know --

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:06.025
Because here's what I got.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:08.528
I have like, you know --
I have like two or three --

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:10.930
I know it's three --
full-sized skeletons.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.065
-Three full-size skeletons.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:14.901
-I have a fake TV
that looks like a '50s TV

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:17.403
that when you turn it on, like,
a hand comes through the screen.

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.972
-Yeah.
-I have my whole family.

00:02:19.972 --> 00:02:23.576
I have 3-D portraits
of every member of my family

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:25.978
from the Haunted Mansion
in Disney World,

00:02:25.978 --> 00:02:27.413
which is cool,
because if you look at it,

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:29.315
like, from one side,
it's your face,

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.183
but if you look at it
from the other side,

00:02:31.183 --> 00:02:33.720
it's the face of a person
who wasted $200.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.888
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:39.558
So, she judges me
for these things.

00:02:39.558 --> 00:02:40.627
But I want to show you -- Okay.

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:41.694
-Is this the first one
you want to show?

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:42.795
-Yeah. Okay.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:44.096
So, let me take you
through these.

00:02:44.096 --> 00:02:45.764
Okay, so, this is the first
thing. This is simple.

00:02:45.764 --> 00:02:49.936
This is a very simple mug

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:51.204
with pumpkins on it
that says "Scary!"

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:52.338
-Yeah.

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:55.441
-Just know that if my house
was on fire

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.343
and I had to choose
between my wedding album

00:02:57.343 --> 00:03:00.279
and this mug,
I would 100% take this mug.

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:01.814
-Got it.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:04.550
-When I saw
this mug in a HomeGoods,

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:10.022
I felt like must be what
like Leonardo DiCaprio

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:12.691
feels like when he sees
a 19-year-old model.

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.027
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:15.027 --> 00:03:17.963
-You had to have it.

00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:21.934
-Because I was like,
"God damn it!

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:25.004
I will have her."

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:28.241
-Is this a Halloween-only mug?
-No. This is -- You know why?

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:30.042
Because it doesn't actually
say anything about Halloween,

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:31.511
so it's it's year round.

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:32.679
It's year round.

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:36.015
And I like it,
because if I were an object,

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:39.418
I would be this mug,
because it says "Scary!",

00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:40.886
but it's not really scary

00:03:40.886 --> 00:03:43.056
and it's a little bit wider
and heavier than you expect.

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:44.256
-Okay.

00:03:44.256 --> 00:03:47.760
-Okay, so, let me see.
So, I'm normal, right?

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.329
That's not a weird thing to own?
-No, that's not a weird thing.

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:51.397
-That's fine. I'm fine.
Okay, okay.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:53.266
-Things are
about to change as far as --

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:56.268
-Okay, because then last year,
I bought this guy.

00:03:56.268 --> 00:04:00.272
-Okay. Let's take a look.
-Okay.

00:04:00.272 --> 00:04:06.245
Now, he is a
nicely dressed scarecrow.

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:10.048
There's nothing alarming --
inherently alarming about him.

00:04:10.048 --> 00:04:13.619
You know, he's maybe
not something a woman purchases

00:04:13.619 --> 00:04:15.455
while her husband is alive.

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:16.889
-Yeah.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:18.858
-Feels more like
something that should be made

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:23.663
for you
by volunteers from the church.

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:26.231
But I bought him. Am I okay?

00:04:26.231 --> 00:04:29.001
-Um, okay.

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:31.136
-It's starting to turn. Okay.
-It's starting to turn.

00:04:31.136 --> 00:04:33.606
-Well --
-Now, this seems -- Can we --

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:35.908
-Yeah, so, this -- Okay,
if you're getting concerned,

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:38.377
things are gonna get worse for
you, because then I went back to

00:04:38.377 --> 00:04:39.678
the same store
and I bought these two.

00:04:39.678 --> 00:04:43.816
-Yeah, definitely --
definitely the same craftsman.

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.618
-Yeah, and I love them.

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:48.420
And, listen,
I had to buy both of them,

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:50.189
because, obviously,
they're a couple.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:51.457
-Yeah.

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:54.260
-Right? And he's
a pumpkin football man,

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.361
and she's a cheerleader

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:57.462
and she's wearing a ring
around her neck,

00:04:57.462 --> 00:05:00.399
so they have clearly made
some sort of chastity promise

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:02.334
to each other.

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:04.470
And, yes, I have used
the football in his hands

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.305
to keep him out
until Thanksgiving.

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:09.141
-Did -- Was this one free,
and then these were each

00:05:09.141 --> 00:05:10.576
like $10,000 each?

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:13.178
Like, it was like a drug dealer?
-It was like a pyramid scheme.

00:05:13.178 --> 00:05:14.780
Yes.

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:16.282
-Okay, now things have turned
for the worse.

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:19.451
-Now even I have to admit
this is problematic.

00:05:19.451 --> 00:05:20.820
Okay, so, I went back to
the same store

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:21.921
and then I bought this guy.

00:05:25.824 --> 00:05:29.295
Why did I buy him?
-Yeah.

00:05:29.295 --> 00:05:35.668
-He looks like
a Victorian child pallbearer,

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:38.504
but he's clearly
a middle-aged gourd.

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:42.875
He has a ring of human hair
that is realistic

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:45.044
and we can only assume
is the hair of his victims.

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:46.579
-Yeah.

00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:52.218
-He is the size of
a humidifier and he costs $60.

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:54.987
-Can I also say one other
problem I have with him?

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:58.023
He has such worse posture.
-Yeah.

00:05:58.023 --> 00:06:02.394
No, even he is sad
that he exists.

00:06:02.394 --> 00:06:03.629
So, this is the final question.

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:08.100
Is Amy right
and I'm crazy or am I okay?

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:10.035
-I think --
Do you want me to say?

00:06:10.035 --> 00:06:11.170
-Yeah.
-I think you're okay.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:16.809
-Oh, okay!
I think you guys know I'm crazy.

00:06:16.809 --> 00:06:19.311
-Also, before you go,
very exciting.

00:06:19.311 --> 00:06:21.547
Girls5eva,
which is a fantastic show...

00:06:21.547 --> 00:06:23.082
-Thank you so much.

00:06:23.082 --> 00:06:25.450
-...has a third season
coming out on Netflix,

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:27.453
and you can also watch the first
two seasons on Netflix.

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:29.621
-Yes. I believe mid-March,
all three seasons

00:06:29.621 --> 00:06:30.856
come out on Netflix.

00:06:30.856 --> 00:06:33.726
It is a great show --
-With a fantastic cast.

00:06:33.726 --> 00:06:35.661
-Yeah. Great Meredith Scardino
wrote it.

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:37.230
Sara Bareilles,
Renée Goldsberry,

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:38.864
Busy Philipps,
and the great Paula Pell.

00:06:38.864 --> 00:06:41.033
-There you go.
You can't go wrong.

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:43.068
You guys, that's Tina Fey.

00:06:43.068 --> 00:06:45.938
"Mean Girls"
in theaters tomorrow.

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:47.639
For info on
the Restless Leg Tour,

00:06:47.639 --> 00:06:49.542
go to tinaamytour.com.

00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:50.910
We'll be right back
with Andrew Scott.

